# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 1 (plan §3 :245 (a)): a named Structure closed by a column-0 bare
# `return` -- Q19.1: a return trailer closes any callable Structure, the named one included -- its
# body holding a statement besides its field.  Construction computes the initializer (book :928)
# and runs no statement of the body: Counter\n reads 4, not 5.  Before, the frame was read as a
# statement of the entry and refused ("assignment target must be a declared typed mutable value").
# Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 4U
    n: n + 1U
return
size_t: got 0U
got: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: got = 4U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
